Z||000000||acquisitiveness||05-02-2000||11:14 AM||||I am going to install a new clutch in my 88 GT T top and would like to know what would be a good clutch set up for the 2.8 or maybe 3.4 ( some day ) 115K on original?? Is it difficult. How would know if an after market or original GM is best. Thanks||||reg||11
Z||000001||fieroshop||05-03-2000||09:53 AM||||Check out my site and click on parts catalog. <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bad88||05-03-2000||09:18 PM||||I put a new clutch in my '88 GT (well the dealer did) but I purchased an aftermarket one which has been working great since.  It's ALOT cheaper than buying the GM clutch and I didn't see any difference between that one and the OEM (the dealer gave it back after installing the new one).  If your planning on doing it yourself, don't waste time trying to install with out pulling the engine.  I tried and there is not enough room to do it on the '88.  Also have your shaft seals changed and the rear engine seal if your so inclined...I'd only want to pull the tranny once in a few years.  Good luck and let me know if you need any more info on cost and all.  (total price was 125.00 for clutch and 800.00 to install)||||reg||6
